# RStudio screen-reader long-file test, long lines (about 200 characters each)
# Each code line carries its number at the end, so you can tell where reading stops.
# RStudio's announced line number is 9 higher than the number in the comment.
# 1. Go to the top: Control+Home (Windows) or Command+Up arrow (Mac).
# 2. Read down with the Down arrow; then, from the top, read continuously: NVDA key+Down arrow
#    (NVDA), Insert+Down arrow (JAWS), or Control+Option+A (VoiceOver).
# 3. Note the last number you hear each way, and whether Down arrow still moves the cursor.
# 4. If NVDA goes silent: NVDA menu, Tools, View log; save the last part of the log.
# Also note your screen reader and its version, and RStudio's (Help, About RStudio).
